  "body": "https://mikewest.github.io/sec-metadata/ is starting to look pretty reasonable. I plan to put up some PRs to sketch out what the integration would look like, based on the thoughts in https://mikewest.github.io/sec-metadata/#fetch-integration. I think we'd need ~3 changes, but who knows? :)\r\n\r\n1.  Add a boolean `user activation` flag to `request` objects, defaulting to `false`. We'd set it in HTML's navigation algorithm, based on whether the navigation was triggered by user activation.\r\n\r\n2.  Call [set the Fetch Metadata headers for a request](https://mikewest.github.io/sec-metadata/#abstract-opdef-set-the-fetch-metadata-headers-for-a-request). Probably from \"main fetch\"?\r\n\r\n3.  Define \"`nested-navigate`\", as per #755.\r\n\r\nWDYT?",
